This adaptation is LGPL-2.1-or-later under the license included above. It models
the fixed Linux reference built with external x86 assembly disabled and inline
MMXEXT enabled; it does not execute MMX instructions or a native FFmpeg process.

The shared coefficient generator also supports arbitrary resize ratios with
on-demand bigint weights instead of support-sized temporary bigint arrays.
resize.ts adapts Q14-to-Q7 horizontal scaling and signed32 vertical accumulation
from libswscale/swscale.c and output.c at the same pinned commit. It uses one
bounded accumulation row and preserves native rounding, wrapping and clipping.

